<title>USA: Clinton seen averting American Air strike-Lindsey.</title>
<headline>Clinton seen averting American Air strike-Lindsey.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>President Bill Clinton was expected on Saturday to act to avert a strike by American Airlines pilots by naming a Presidential Emergency Board (PEB) to study the dispute, a top White House official said.</p>
<p>&quot;My sense is he will ... issue a PEB,&quot; White House Deputy Counsel Bruce Lindsey told reporters. By naming a PEB, the president would postpone any walkout for 60 days at American, a unit of Fort Worth-based AMR Corp.</p>
</text>
